MNIST Handwritten Digit Recognition

Project Overview

This project uses machine learning to recognize handwritten digits (0–9) from images using the MNIST dataset.

A Streamlit web application allows users to upload an image of a handwritten digit and receive a prediction.

Dataset

* Dataset: MNIST
* Images: 70,000
* Image dimensions: 28 × 28 pixels
* Classes: Digits 0–9
* Pixel values normalized between 0 and 1

Machine Learning Algorithms

Three algorithms were evaluated:

1. K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
2. Support Vector Machine (LinearSVC)
3. Random Forest Classifier

Model Comparison

Model	Accuracy
KNN	95.00%
SVM (LinearSVC)	88.55%
Random Forest	97.25%

The models were evaluated on the same sample of 2,000 test images. Random Forest achieved the highest accuracy in this comparison.

